{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-schrodinger-jet-coaction","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:schrodinger-jet-coaction","kind":"remark","title":"q-Deformed Schrodinger equation","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-q-reeb-vector-field","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-harmonic-form","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-heisenberg-commutator","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-main-commutative-diagram"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-q-harmonic-form","tags":["schrodinger","q-deformation","jet-bundle"],"text":"schrodinger-jet-coaction.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:schrodinger-jet-coaction\"></a><p>For a section <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\psi \\in \\Gamma(\\mathcal{S}_{\\mathrm{lin}})</code>, the Schrödinger dynamics dictate</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  J\\hbar_q(p)\\iota_{\\xi_q} D_A \\psi =  \\hat{H}_q \\psi,</code></pre>\n<p>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\hat{H}_q = -\\tfrac{1}{2}\\hbar_q\\Delta_q + V_q</code> is the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>-deformed Hamiltonian. The local quantum Planck constant is <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\hbar_q(p) = 1 - q(p)^{-1}</code>. Contracting <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">D_A\\psi</code> with the Reeb vector field <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\xi_q</code> produces a section of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{S}_{\\mathrm{lin}}</code>. As <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q(p) \\to 1</code>, uncertainty vanishes and the wave trajectory freezes classically.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/schrodinger-jet-coaction.md","heading":"Remark","number":"3.27.3"}
